// The kinded type component — the pathological pin for a form that parses and
// is declined by name.
//
// GRADUATION: this block PARSES and its lowering DECLINES it. `type Hom : Ob ->
// Ob -> Type` declares a type FAMILY of arity two, which the dependent-types
// rung elaborates; until it does, the lowerer refuses it by name
// (`LowerError::KindedTypeComponent`).
//
// WHY THE PIN EXISTS. The form previously had no grammar production at all, so
// a signature member whose tail matched no alternative let the field consume
// what followed it. A decline with no corpus witness silently regresses into a
// drop later and nothing catches it, so the pin is the witness that the refusal
// is still a refusal.
//
// WHAT SEPARATES THE TWO FORMS. `type T : κ` and `type T = τ` differ by one
// character and put a type in the same field. Reading the first as the second
// would bind `T` to a type its source does not state — an engine limit recorded
// as author intent. The manifest component below must therefore still
// elaborate while the kinded one is refused; a gate that refused both would
// pass a test written only against the refusal.
//
// Parse-only here (the PBG zero-obligation sweep is this tree's only gate); the
// decline and its separating pair are witnessed by `surface-engine`
// `tests/acceptance.rs`.

// The kinded component: a type family, declined by name.
module Indexed : #{ type Hom : Integer -> Integer } { }

// The manifest component, one character apart, which still elaborates.
module Manifest : #{ type Hom = Integer } { }
